# Prepositions and the verb "come" that stand before a season word and name
# the season, never a verb: "since fall", "around fall", "come fall". They
# add to the connectors "in", "from", "to", "until", "during", "by", "of",
# "before" and "after", which license the season too.
around
come
for
into
since
through
toward
towards
